        "text": "Hello, I’m Hannah, and I help run a repair café in Bristol. People bring in things that have stopped working, and our volunteers try to fix them together with their owners. When we started, I imagined we’d need a proper workshop. In fact, finding somewhere warm and easy to reach mattered more. We initially arranged to use the church hall, but its heating broke down just before our first session, so we ended up using the library. It turned out to be a better choice. People who were already there to borrow books came over to see what we were doing."
