        "speaker": "Hannah",
        "text": "In the beginning, I thought most visitors would bring phones. We do see a few, though manufacturers can make them difficult to open. The biggest increase has actually been in lamps. Quite often the lamp itself is fine, and it’s the switch or the cable that needs attention. Of course, we check anything electrical carefully before somebody takes it home. We also look at clothes, toys and small pieces of furniture. One volunteer fixed a child’s wooden chair in ten minutes, after its owner had been convinced it was beyond saving."
